qx|A5|st||rh||ah|Board 5 IMPs   -    February 28, 2024|pn|hondo717,IraCT,adriennek,danpsych|
md|3SQT72HAQT6DAJCJ72,SKJ983H98DQ4CAT43,SA5H543DKT9873CK6,S64HKJ72D652CQ985|sv|n|
mb|2D|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I agree with opening 2@D. My philosophy is there is no gap between a weak 2 and a 1 bid. If, with a 6-card suit, you are too weak to open at the 1-level, then you should open at the 2-level.|
PG| ***** 88 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|However, some might reasonably feel that with an outside A and K, the hand has too much defense to open a weak 2 but it is not strong enough to open 1. That is a reasonable thought although I still personally open 2@D.|
PG| ***** 89 ***** |


